  "downloads": 2860,
  "description": "<h3><strong>Live Like Experience - A SAIN Preset</strong></h3>\n<h3><strong><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://discord.com/channels/875684761291599922/1403070451449725028\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Discord Thread</a></strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Provides manageable Scavs. They aren’t usually fearsome warriors, but ignore them long enough and they might get lucky.</li>\n<li>PMC’s are a threat. A healthy mix of Chads and Normal players. They will be an issue.</li>\n<li>Bosses and followers exist to be a challenge.</li>\n<li>AI hearing is turned wayyyy down, the goal is to keep them from starring at walls and sitting in cover forever.</li>\n<li>AI has some minor map specific tuning. For example, labs will see must more aggressive play than shoreline.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Overall this preset aims to provide a “Live Like Experience”. Some raids will be easy, some raids you’ll run into a super sweaty giga chad. Boss fights should be a challenge while scavs should usually be easy kills. I’m a believer of “if you’re surviving every raid because the fights are a joke than it’s not fun” camp, so expect to die sometimes.</p>\n<p>This preset is what I play with, I’m a 30 something dad gamer with a military background. So the goal is fun, semi-realistic, and not soul crushing.</p>\n<h3>Install</h3>\n<p>1. Drag and drop like the below image.</p>\n<p>2. In-game press F6 to open the SAIN menu and ensure Live Like Experience is selected. Click save in the top right.</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.imgur.com/vKRw58b.gif\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/vKRw58b.gif\" alt=\"vKRw58b.gif\" /></a></p>\n<p>Feel free to buy me an overpriced starbucks flat white - <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://ko-fi.com/shibdib\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https://ko-fi.com/shibdib</a></p>\n<p><em>This is under active development, I will provide updates as needed. Please provide feedback via comments.</em></p>\n",
